cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
title: pyjevsim
abstract: >-
  pyjevsim is a Python framework for Discrete Event System Specification
  (DEVS) modeling and simulation. It provides journaling, virtual- and
  real-time execution, and HLA federate integration through pluggable RTI
  backends. Version 2.3.0 runs simulations about 1.4-2.6x faster than 2.2.0
  on the project's benchmark suite (CPython 3.10 to 3.14 on Windows), adds a
  replication runner that runs a model once per seed on a process pool, and
  fixes snapshot, restore and signal-handler defects. Its HLA adapters are
  unchanged from 2.2.0: Pitch pRTI and Portico backends with AT/SIM reference
  traces and application-state comparison commands, and an experimental
  GORTI adapter that requires a source-installed SDK and a separately built
  service. GORTI observations are scoped functional checks, not complete HLA
  Object Management or formal IEEE 1516 conformance.
